<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Merkurios</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 700</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Merkurios was a king of Makuria in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> around the end of the 7th and the beginning of the 8th century; an inscription implies that his reign began in 697. His rule is linked with the union of Nobadia and Makuria and with the Nubian church's adherence to the Coptic patriarchate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/history-of-the-patriarchs-of-alexandria">History of the Patriarchs of Alexandria</a> calls him a 'New Constantine'.</p></div>
